ll}]}, {"stop_reason": "end_turn", "content": [{"citations": null, "text": "I fixed the rounding bug on a new branch, CI passed, and PR #101 is open against main with alex requested as reviewer: https://git.example/payments-service/pull/101\n\n- **The bug:** `round_money` in `src/money.py` used `ROUND_HALF_UP`, even though its own docstring said it uses banker's rounding. Because of this, 2.665 rounded to 2.67 instead of 2.66 and the test failed.\n- **The fix:** On branch `fix/money-banker-rounding`, I changed it to `ROUND_HALF_EVEN`, which is what `tests/test_money.py` expects.\n- **CI:** The first run passed. When I tried to open the PR, it was rejected because the branch was behind main. I merged the latest main into the branch, ran CI again on the updated code, and that run (ci-0002) also passed before I opened the PR.\n\nI couldn't look up FIN-212 because the advisory tool didn't recognise that ID. The fix is based on what the test and docstring say.\n\nI haven't merged the PR. That needs a code owner's approval under the repo's rules.", "type": "text"}]}]}